From: OpenWrt RN01 port <nobody@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5332: add wcss multipd + wifi nodes

IPQ5332 runs its Wi-Fi firmware on an on-SoC Hexagon (Q6) using the
multi protection domain (multipd) model: a root PD (q6_fw0) plus one
user PD per radio.  Add the pieces the multipd remoteproc driver
(qcom,ipq5332-q6-mpd) and the ath12k AHB driver (qcom,ipq5332-wifi)
need:

 - the wcss smp2p edge (master-kernel/slave-kernel entries) used for
   fatal/ready/spawn/stop handshakes with the Q6,
 - the root remoteproc@d100000 node with its glink-edge and the two
   user PD child nodes pd-1 (AHB radio) and pd-2 (companion radio),
 - the Q6/WCSS reserved-memory carve-outs (q6 region, m3 dump, caldb,
   MLO global memory),
 - wifi0, the internal 2.4 GHz AHB radio, and wifi1, the QCN6432
   companion radio.

All register addresses, GIC SPI numbers, smp2p bit indices and reserved
memory offsets are transcribed from the vendor device tree of a shipping
IPQ5332 board (Xiaomi RN01).  Everything is left disabled; boards opt in.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt RN01 port <nobody@openwrt.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5332.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5332.dtsi
@@ -158,6 +158,55 @@
 			no-map;
 
 			hwlocks = <&tcsr_mutex 3>;
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Q6/WCSS carve-outs.  The layout below is transcribed from the
+		 * vendor device tree of a 512 MiB IPQ5332 board; q6_region is
+		 * the umbrella region the root PD loads its code/data into and
+		 * it deliberately overlaps q6_ipq5332_data, exactly as the
+		 * vendor DT does (the per-radio regions are sub-ranges of the
+		 * Q6 window).  Boards with a different DRAM size or a single
+		 * radio should override these.
+		 */
+		q6_region: q6-region@4a900000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4a900000 0x0 0x2100000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		q6_ipq5332_data: q6-ipq5332-data@4bd00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4bd00000 0x0 0xd00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		m3_dump: m3-dump@4ca00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4ca00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		q6_caldb: q6-caldb@4cb00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4cb00000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		q6_qcn6432_data: q6-qcn6432-data@4ce00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4ce00000 0x0 0xe00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		m3_dump_qcn6432: m3-dump-qcn6432@4dc00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4dc00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		q6_caldb_qcn6432: q6-caldb-qcn6432@4dd00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4dd00000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		mlo_global_mem: mlo-global-mem@4e000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4e000000 0x0 0x700000>;
+			no-map;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -653,7 +702,213 @@
 				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 14 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 				frame-number = <6>;
 				status = "disabled";
+			};
+		};
+
